{
  "title": "The て-form",
  "note": "る-verbs drop る and add て: 食べる → 食べて. う-verbs change by ending: う, つ, る → って; む, ぶ, ぬ → んで; く → いて; ぐ → いで; す → して. Irregular: 行く → 行って, する → して, 来る → 来て. Uses: てください (please do), ています (is doing; ongoing state), and linking actions in order.",
  "src": {
    "t": "Tae Kim's Guide: Compound Sentences (the て-form)",
    "u": "https://guidetojapanese.org/learn/grammar/compound"
  },
